<title>BELGIUM: SIDRO H1 1996 PROFIT DOUBLES ON SALE.</title>
<headline>SIDRO H1 1996 PROFIT DOUBLES ON SALE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996 (in</p>
<p>millions of Belgian francs unless stated):</p>
<p>    Cons net profit	 215  vs  112</p>
<p>    Cons current income    96  vs   93</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gains   106  vs   36</p>
<p>NOTE - Sidro is a Belgian holding company with interests in</p>
<p>a number of petroleum companies.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said the sharp rise in earnings</p>
<p>was mainly due to a reduction in its stake in United Meridian</p>
<p>Corp. that resulted in a large capital gain. It did not</p>
<p>provide details. At the end of 1995, it held 1.1 percent of UMC.</p>
<p>Sidro said first half earnings did not permit it to make any</p>
<p>prediction about full year profit but said that, barring</p>
<p>unforeseen circumstands, it should pay a dividend at least equal</p>
<p>to 1995's 80 francs</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
